1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,880
Hi everyone, I am Ujwal.

2
00:00:03,760 --> 00:00:06,080
Sunita's father died last year,

3
00:00:06,080 --> 00:00:10,495
leaving a tin of old papers: a passbook, an insurance bond,

4
00:00:10,495 --> 00:00:11,992
a share certificate.

5
00:00:11,992 --> 00:00:13,315
The money is hers.

6
00:00:13,315 --> 00:00:16,378
The hard part is discovering where it is,

7
00:00:16,378 --> 00:00:17,872
and how to claim it.

8
00:00:18,720 --> 00:00:19,891
This is Virasat.

9
00:00:19,891 --> 00:00:23,290
Photograph the papers, and it finds the money,

10
00:00:23,290 --> 00:00:27,576
explains what to do in your language, and fills the forms.

11
00:00:28,440 --> 00:00:31,844
Virasat turns each paper into structured fields,

12
00:00:31,844 --> 00:00:34,256
every one with its own confidence.

13
00:00:34,256 --> 00:00:38,311
Three forgotten papers become three places where money is

14
00:00:38,311 --> 00:00:38,880
waiting.

15
00:00:39,760 --> 00:00:43,684
But Virasat can find something more important: the account

16
00:00:43,684 --> 00:00:45,443
that was never in the tin.

17
00:00:45,443 --> 00:00:49,177
A legal heir can obtain the account holder's income tax

18
00:00:49,177 --> 00:00:49,856
statement.

19
00:00:49,855 --> 00:00:53,768
Virasat reads it for every bank and company that paid him,

20
00:00:53,768 --> 00:00:57,343
revealing accounts that never appeared in her papers.

21
00:00:57,343 --> 00:01:00,151
We are not just digitising what she found.

22
00:01:00,151 --> 00:01:03,160
We are helping her discover what was missing.

23
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:05,696
Real records are messy.

24
00:01:05,696 --> 00:01:09,005
Names appear differently across institutions,

25
00:01:09,005 --> 00:01:11,799
so when the full name is too specific,

26
00:01:11,799 --> 00:01:15,329
a broader search finds it: three years of unpaid

27
00:01:15,329 --> 00:01:16,064
dividends.

28
00:01:16,920 --> 00:01:20,905
Three simple questions determine her route: nominee,

29
00:01:20,905 --> 00:01:22,515
legal heir, or court.

30
00:01:22,515 --> 00:01:24,935
That decision is not made by AI.

31
00:01:24,935 --> 00:01:28,994
It comes from an open rule corpus: each institution's

32
00:01:28,994 --> 00:01:32,823
claim process, written down, versioned and tested,

33
00:01:32,823 --> 00:01:36,806
with the rule id shown so the decision is traceable.

34
00:01:36,806 --> 00:01:41,040
Then the documents she needs, and where to get each one.

35
00:01:41,920 --> 00:01:46,570
Before Sunita acts, Virasat challenges its own guidance.

36
00:01:46,570 --> 00:01:50,805
One AI looks for problems, like this name mismatch.

37
00:01:50,806 --> 00:01:54,596
Another reviews it, and can only add caution,

38
00:01:54,596 --> 00:01:56,702
never override the rules.

39
00:01:56,702 --> 00:01:59,608
Sunita reads the reasoning herself.

40
00:02:00,480 --> 00:02:03,700
Now everything becomes something she can use.

41
00:02:03,700 --> 00:02:07,174
One click creates her claim form, the checklist,

42
00:02:07,174 --> 00:02:09,996
and cover letters in English and Hindi.

43
00:02:09,996 --> 00:02:14,054
Virasat tracks it, and prepares the escalation if nobody

44
00:02:14,054 --> 00:02:15,720
replies in thirty days.

45
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:19,570
And it is not built only for people comfortable with

46
00:02:19,570 --> 00:02:20,787
financial websites.

47
00:02:20,787 --> 00:02:22,911
The whole journey works in Hindi,

48
00:02:22,911 --> 00:02:26,257
and the guidance is read aloud for anyone who is not

49
00:02:26,257 --> 00:02:27,544
comfortable reading.

50
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:29,815
The economics work.

51
00:02:29,815 --> 00:02:33,912
Serving one family costs about thirty six rupees of AI.

52
00:02:33,913 --> 00:02:38,063
The average returned at Gujarat's camps is thirty eight

53
00:02:38,063 --> 00:02:39,798
thousand seven hundred.

54
00:02:39,798 --> 00:02:44,118
And the Vault checks that today's accounts have nominees,

55
00:02:44,118 --> 00:02:48,059
so tomorrow's money does not become another family's

56
00:02:48,059 --> 00:02:48,589
search.

57
00:02:48,589 --> 00:02:50,377
Find what was forgotten.

58
00:02:50,377 --> 00:02:51,867
Claim what is yours.

59
00:02:51,867 --> 00:02:52,463
Virasat.

60
00:02:52,463 --> 00:02:54,176
Your money, your right.

61
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:55,976
Thank you.
